INT. WITCH'S TOWER - SPIRAL STAIR - NIGHT

Stone. Torchlight. Wind howling through arrow slits.

ZEPHYRINE, 50, witch, robes patched with stolen feathers, climbs backward, pointing a staff down the stairwell. BRYNJA, 30, knight, dented plate, longsword out, climbs forward, pushing up.

They meet at a landing and stop.

BRYNJA
You're the witch.

ZEPHYRINE
You're the knight.

BRYNJA
You're under arrest.

ZEPHYRINE
Under what?

BRYNJA
The king's law.

ZEPHYRINE
Which king?

Brynja's sword drops an inch. She hadn't thought about that.

BRYNJA
The one with the crown.

ZEPHYRINE
He's been dead nine years.

Brynja steps up one stair. Zephyrine raises the staff. A spark jumps from the tip and sizzles across the stone.

BRYNJA
Don't.

ZEPHYRINE
Then don't push.

Brynja pushes. She grabs the staff and wrenches it to one side. The spark lands on a torch, which flares. Both stumble. She tumbles into a wall, but she keeps hold of the staff.

ZEPHYRINE (CONT'D)
That's mine.

BRYNJA
Not anymore.

Zephyrine kicks her in the shin. Brynja yelps and lets go. Zephyrine seizes the staff, and now they stand eye to eye, panting.

BRYNJA (CONT'D)
Why did you steal the bell?

ZEPHYRINE
It was singing in her sleep.

BRYNJA
Whose?

ZEPHYRINE
Yours. Your daughter's.

The wind quiets. Brynja steps back. The sword lowers fully.

BRYNJA
How do you know that?

Zephyrine looks at her for a long time.

ZEPHYRINE
Come up. I'll show you.

She turns and climbs. Brynja, shoulders heavy, sheathes the sword and follows.
